--TEST--
A class that implements `KeyedIterator<K, V>` must declare `key()`, so a class with only `advance()` and `current()` does not compile — `rule:iteration/keyed-interfaces`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: KeyedIterator
// This class has `advance` and `current` but no `key`, so it does not compile.
final class NoKey implements KeyedIterator<string, int> {
    public function advance(): bool {
        return false;
    }

    public function current(): int {
        return 0;
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0449]: `NoKey` does not declare `key`, which `KeyedIterator` requires
  --> case.nvs:4:13
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
